Chapter: ProseSmoke

 Combined prose tests: record/variant with prose, bracket notation
 in prose, and a greeting function with prose documentation.

 A ProseBasic is a record containing:
 - value : Integer
 - label : Text

 ProseResult is one of:
 - Ok carrying an Integer
 - Err carrying a Text

 We say:

Section: Types

  ProseBasic = record {
   value : Integer,
   label : Text
  }

  ProseResult =
   | Ok (Integer)
   | Err (Text)

 To add-values (a) (b) gives an Integer:

Section: Functions

  add-values : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add-values (a) (b) = a + b

 such that the result is always the sum of the inputs.

 To describe (pb) gives a Text:

  describe : ProseBasic -> Text
  describe (pb) = pb.label & ": " & show (pb.value)

 For every ProseBasic, the description contains the label.

  show-result : ProseResult -> Text
  show-result (r) = when r
   is Ok (n) -> "ok:" & show n
   is Err (msg) -> "err:" & msg

 Memory layout at 0x100000:
 [0] field-a   i32
 [4] field-b   i32
 [8] field-c   i64

  field-sum : Integer
  field-sum = 0 + 4 + 8

 To greet (name) gives a greeting:

  greet : Text -> Text
  greet (name) = "Hello, " & name & "!"

Section: Body

 [tag] bracket prose directly above a definition:
  opening : Text =
   let pb = ProseBasic { value = add-values 10 32, label = "answer" }
   in let desc = describe pb
   in let r1 = show-result (Ok 42)
   in let r2 = show-result (Err "not found")
   in desc & "\n" & r1 & "\n" & r2 & "\nfields-" & show field-sum & "\n" & greet "World"

